%description:

Tcp.synRetries:passive -- the SYN-ACK goes this many times again, and then the passive open gives up.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the retransmissions of a SYN or of a SYN-ACK, after which the open
fails (Linux net.ipv4.tcp_syn_retries [...]; Linux has tcp_synack_retries for the SYN-ACK)".

The classes: retries (1 and more; 12 is the default, 6 the value of LinuxTcp), with a facet for
the SYN of an active open and one for the SYN-ACK of a passive open; zero (0). The code:
TcpConnection::process_TIMEOUT_SYN_REXMIT() gives up when the count of retransmissions
exceeds the value. This test separates the facet from "zero": with 0, the
SYN-ACK goes only once.

Host under test: host2, the passive opener; the tap drops each segment of host1 after the SYN,
so the handshake never completes at host2. Observation: level 1, three SYN-ACKs of host2.

%# parameter: Tcp.synRetries
%# class: passive
%# value: 2
%# key: *.host2.tcp.synRetries
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSynRetriesPassive")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false").drop()
                     .describe("each segment of host1 after its SYN"))
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
        }))
        .meanwhile(exactlyTimes(3, on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                       .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
                                       .describe("a SYN-ACK of host2")
                                       .within(9.0)));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSynRetriesPassive compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.synRetries = 2    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSynRetriesPassive: PASS
